{# Above-the-fold font preloads: body text (Thmanyah Sans Regular),
   medium-weight UI text (category chips, buttons: Thmanyah Sans Medium),
   and numerals/Latin (Inter). Found via a Lighthouse LCP audit: Medium
   wasn't preloaded, so the browser only discovered it after parsing CSS,
   adding a chained request on the critical path. See docs/design-system.md. #}
<link rel="preload" href="/fonts/inter/inter-variable-latin.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" href="/fonts/thmanyah/thmanyahsans-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" href="/fonts/thmanyah/thmanyahsans-Medium.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
{# Bold weights: the public menu's restaurant-name <h1> (serif display) and
   every menu item card title (sans) both render bold, above the fold, in
   Arabic -- measured via Lighthouse as the cause of a 3.5s+ LCP on the
   Arabic menu vs ~2s in English (Phase 8 audit): without a preload, the
   browser only discovers these two files after parsing app.css, adding a
   full extra round trip to the critical path that the English page (Inter,
   already preloaded) never pays. #}
<link rel="preload" href="/fonts/thmanyah/thmanyahsans-Bold.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" href="/fonts/thmanyah/thmanyahserifdisplay-Bold.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>

<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/app.css">
<script defer src="/js/vendor/htmx.min.js"></script>
{# Alpine's CDN build starts via a queued microtask right after its own
   script executes, not on DOMContentLoaded -- so a later <script defer>
   that calls Alpine.store()/registers an alpine:init listener runs too
   late and finds Alpine already started (every $store.* reference then
   throws "Cannot read properties of undefined"). Any page that needs to
   register a store or plugin before Alpine scans the DOM must inject its
   script tags earlier via a `pre_alpine_scripts` block defined directly
   in that page's *layout* file (e.g. layouts/menu.njk), not here --
   a block defined inside this included partial isn't reachable from a
   page template that extends a different layout (verified empirically;
   Nunjucks blocks resolve against the direct extends chain only, not
   through an unrelated {% include %}). #}
<script defer src="/js/vendor/alpine.min.js"></script>
<style>[x-cloak] { display: none !important; }</style>
